WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.895
morning the diner was extra busy.

2
00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:24.760
Ally, Flo, and Barry dashed from table to table taking orders, and Randy and Ray cooked nonstop in

3
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:25.200
the kitchen.

4
00:00:30.508 --> 00:00:34.230
"There are so many unfamiliar faces in here," Ally said to Flo.

5
00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.072
"Are they all bird-watchers in town to look for the whoopers?"

6
00:00:38.092 --> 00:00:42.334
"They don't look like bird-watchers to me," Flo replied.

7
00:00:42.354 --> 00:00:45.376
"They'd have binoculars and field guides."

8
00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:48.658
"Maybe there's a convention," Ally said.

9
00:00:48.678 --> 00:00:52.680
"I'll ask those people at table five before I take their order."

10
00:00:58.603 --> 00:01:01.308
folks, welcome to Ray's," Ally said.

11
00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:03.590
"What brings you all to town?"

12
00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.472
"We're here looking for a scoop," a tall man replied.

13
00:01:07.492 --> 00:01:10.193
"Oh, so you want ice cream for breakfast?"

14
00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:11.034
Ally asked.

15
00:01:11.054 --> 00:01:15.216
"We have vanilla, chocolate "No!"

16
00:01:16.236 --> 00:01:16.937
The man laughed.

17
00:01:17.437 --> 00:01:20.399
"We're reporters, so a scoop for us is a big news story.

18
00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:22.920
We're here to cover Lainie Polk's P.O.D.

19
00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.162
launch." "The rumors are true?

20
00:01:26.882 --> 00:01:29.083
Lainie Polk is launching her P.O.D.

21
00:01:29.123 --> 00:01:30.024
from Sandville?"

22
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.921
Ally could hardly contain her excitement.

23
00:01:32.941 --> 00:01:34.401
"Do you know when?

24
00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.222
How many passengers can she take?"

25
00:01:36.242 --> 00:01:37.522
"Hold up!

26
00:01:38.802 --> 00:01:40.443
We're usually the ones who ask the questions!"

27
00:01:40.943 --> 00:01:41.803
the reporter said.

28
00:01:41.823 --> 00:01:44.484
"Sorry, that's all the information we have right now.

29
00:01:44.924 --> 00:01:49.385
But if Lainie Polk does show up in town, we'll be standing by, waiting to cover the story."

30
00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:54.847
Ally had trouble concentrating as she worked.

31
00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:59.388
All she could think about was getting back to a planet in her own solar system.

32
00:02:01.036 --> 00:02:06.538
"As long as we land on an inhabited planet, I'll find a comm device and call my parents.

33
00:02:07.358 --> 00:02:08.978
Gosh, I have so much to tell them.

34
00:02:09.398 --> 00:02:10.839
I won't even know where to begin."

35
00:02:10.859 --> 00:02:15.040
"Excuse me," a customer at the counter called.

36
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.361
"Do you have any cupcakes today, or did they all fall on the floor?"

37
00:02:21.622 --> 00:02:24.422
Ally was confused until she recognized the customer.

38
00:02:25.943 --> 00:02:29.784
It was the woman from the other day, the one who'd caught the tray of cupcakes.

39
00:02:32.813 --> 00:02:33.814
"Oh, hi again."

40
00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:34.995
Ally smiled.

41
00:02:35.015 --> 00:02:39.238
"Are you in town for Lainie Polk's announcement too?"

42
00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:41.279
The customer shook her head.

43
00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:45.402
"It sure seems like everyone else is, doesn't it?"

44
00:02:48.905 --> 00:02:50.326
She looked closely at Ally.

45
00:02:50.346 --> 00:02:54.489
"Are you interested in space travel?"

46
00:02:54.509 --> 00:02:58.512
"Yes!" Ally exclaimed.

47
00:02:59.476 --> 00:03:01.377
"It's the only way I'll ever get home again!"

48
00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:06.361
She gasped and slapped her hand over her mouth.

49
00:03:07.201 --> 00:03:08.622
"Why did I say that out loud?"

50
00:03:09.023 --> 00:03:09.463
she thought.

51
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:12.985
"It's almost like that customer made me say it!"

52
00:03:14.506 --> 00:03:18.589
That's when Ally remembered the difference between Carparians and Camparians.

53
00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:23.993
"Carparians are shape-shifters," Ally's teacher had explained.

54
00:03:24.013 --> 00:03:28.716
"They have the power to make others tell the truth just by looking in their eyes.

55
00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:32.979
But Carparians are very different from Astralians.

56
00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:39.344
They are an aggressive species who enjoy creating mayhem, not peace, on other planets."

57
00:03:43.407 --> 00:03:48.111
"Um Ally gulped and avoided making eye contact with the customer.

58
00:03:48.131 --> 00:03:50.493
"I think I hear Ray calling me in the kitchen.

59
00:03:50.954 --> 00:03:51.714
I'll be right back."

60
00:03:54.196 --> 00:03:56.718
Ally scurried into the kitchen and grabbed Barry.

61
00:03:57.459 --> 00:03:58.640
"I have to make a phone call.

62
00:03:58.924 --> 00:04:01.345
Can you please take the order of that customer at the counter?"

63
00:04:01.365 --> 00:04:03.425
"Sure thing," Barry said.

64
00:04:06.026 --> 00:04:09.747
Ally ducked behind the door and watched as Barry took the customer's order.

65
00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:16.669
"If she is a Carparian," Ally thought, "maybe she'll make Barry blurt something out too!"

66
00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.911
But the customer simply gave Barry her order and then went back to reading on her phone.

67
00:04:25.072 --> 00:04:26.252
Ally sighed in relief.

68
00:04:27.832 --> 00:04:31.734
"There was nothing strange about her interaction with Barry," she told herself.

69
00:04:31.754 --> 00:04:35.176
"My imagination is working overtime again."

70
00:04:40.439 --> 00:04:42.100
Ally headed back into the dining room.

71
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:43.681
Ping! Ping!

72
00:04:43.721 --> 00:04:47.263
Ping! Just then all the customers' phones began pinging.

73
00:04:47.843 --> 00:04:51.405
Everyone, except for the woman at the counter, got up and rushed for the door.

74
00:04:53.786 --> 00:04:55.987
Ally stopped the tall reporter on his way out.

75
00:04:56.007 --> 00:04:57.168
"What's going on?"

76
00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:02.070
"Lainie Polk is holding a press conference at the UFO Museum in an hour," he said.

77
00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.172
"I knew she was in Sandville, and I'm never wrong!"

78
00:05:06.633 --> 00:05:07.693
He rushed out the door.

79
00:05:07.713 --> 00:05:09.975
"In one hour?"

80
00:05:10.515 --> 00:05:11.996
Ally thought, looking at the clock.

81
00:05:13.337 --> 00:05:17.799
She still had three hours left on her shift, but she had to get to that press conference.

82
00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.062
"Flo, can you cover for me for a few hours?"

83
00:05:22.542 --> 00:05:23.102
Ally asked.

84
00:05:23.903 --> 00:05:24.583
Flo shrugged.

85
00:05:25.183 --> 00:05:26.044
"No problem.

86
00:05:26.452 --> 00:05:30.135
We were really busy before, but now this place is practically empty."

87
00:05:30.155 --> 00:05:33.618
"Thanks, I owe you one!"

88
00:05:34.319 --> 00:05:37.221
Ally took off her apron and ran outside to call Mateo.

89
00:05:37.782 --> 00:05:40.444
Before she could dial his number, her own phone rang.

90
00:05:41.405 --> 00:05:42.125
It was Mateo.

91
00:05:42.145 --> 00:05:44.728
"Meet me at the museum—as fast as you can!"
